window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-52aafd6a320b9efa"]={"key":"ny_main-52aafd6a320b9efa","group":"ny_main","uid":"52aafd6a320b9efa","rank":49,"title":"granthill cavendish referral compliance assessment","occupation":"medical_health_services_managers","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are the medical and health services manager at Granthill Laboratories, and Thandiwe Sorensen needs a finished compliance assessment by close of business Friday so Genevieve Lindqvist can decide whether to approve publication of Cavendish Engineering’s patient-referral handling review for a broad, non-specialist audience. The attached file, `cavendish_referral_controls_and_records.pdf`, is the only source for this work: it contains the applicable internal controls, definitions, publication conditions, and anonymized operational referral records. The records are incomplete in places, and the policy distinguishes mandatory evidence from recommended practice without making the boundary obvious in every borderline case. A full case-by-case review cannot be completed before Friday, so I need a defensible, bounded assessment rather than an unqualified impression or a request to postpone the work. Write `cavendish_referral_compliance_assessment.docx` into the top level of the working directory the solver starts in, using exactly that filename. Please make the document no more than two pages and suitable for someone who understands ordinary workplace language but is not a compliance specialist. For (1), state the purpose, the review scope, the evidence period or as-of point, and what part of the supplied records was actually considered; make the limits of coverage understandable to Genevieve. For (2), assess the relevant referral-handling controls in the supplied policy and state which requirements are supported as compliant, which are not established from the available evidence, and which are contradicted by the records, keeping those conclusions tied to what the source actually shows. For (3), treat the policy’s mandatory and recommended language carefully in the findings, especially where a missing or late record could be read either way, and do not silently turn good practice into a compulsory requirement. For (4), explain the fallback used because time rules out a complete review, including why its coverage is reasonable, what remains outside it, and how far the resulting claims can safely extend; do not present a limited review as proof that every referral was handled correctly. For (5), give a concise evidence summary that lets a reader follow the important findings without reproducing patient details, and use source locators, record groupings, or other privacy-minimized references rather than identifiable case information. For (6), protect confidentiality throughout: do not include patient names, direct identifiers, unnecessary clinical details, or invented facts, rates, dates, or policy requirements, and do not make a clinical or legal claim that the packet cannot support. For (7), finish with one clear decision about what publication, if any, is supportable under the controls, with the scope and limitations of that decision stated plainly; do not offer several equal alternatives or replace the decision with a generic disclaimer. For (8), keep the prose specific and unambiguous, define any technical term a general reader needs, and make sure the conclusion agrees with the findings and does not end as a list of unrelated future tasks. This is a completed artifact for approval and downstream publication, not a description of how you would perform the assessment, and no internet research is needed.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/cavendish_referral_controls_and_records.pdf` — The sole evidence source for the assessment: it contains the internal referral-handling control standard, the mandatory-versus-recommended definitions, publication conditions, and anonymized operational records with incomplete and borderline evidence.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `cavendish_referral_compliance_assessment.docx` — A concise, privacy-minimized compliance assessment for Genevieve Lindqvist’s publication decision, written for a broad non-specialist audience. (Write the file into the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.; No more than two pages.; Base all factual findings on the supplied PDF.; Distinguish compliant, not established, and contradicted findings.; Do not reproduce patient names, direct identifiers, or unnecessary clinical details.; State one bounded publication decision and its evidentiary limitations.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/cavendish_referral_controls_and_records.pdf","bytes":23190,"extension":".pdf","url":"assets/27dff23041703ea7e71b90eb0e85737c99a23fb21d01e7cada02317b2fef47b7.pdf","sha256":"27dff23041703ea7e71b90eb0e85737c99a23fb21d01e7cada02317b2fef47b7","preview":{"kind":"pdf","text":"GRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                                           Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n Cavendish Engineering referral-handling review\n Internal control standard and de-identified operational record packet\n\n                          Document owner               Referral Operations                                              Issued                        17 Jul 2026\n\n                          Evidence period              01 Apr 2026 to 30 Jun 2026                                       Evidence cut-off              30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local\n\n                          Record population            32 referral records in the operational extract                   Handling team                 Cavendish Engineering Referral Operations\n\n\n\n\n 1. Purpose and scope\n This packet sets the internal referral-handling controls used for Cavendish Engineering's review and supplies the de-identified operational evidence available at the stated cut-off. It covers referrals\n received by the Referral Operations team during the evidence period. The packet contains no clinical assessment and no patient names or direct identifiers.\n\n The record population is split into four workflow groups: external transfers closed by the cut-off (8 records); external transfers awaiting receiving-service confirmation (8); internal coordination, both closed\n and open (8); and referrals returned before any external disclosure (8). A record marked Pending receipt or Open is not a closed referral at the cut-off.\n\n 2. Evidence terms\n                          Term                                     Meaning in this packet\n\n                          Compliant                                Direct record evidence supports every applicable part of the mandatory control.\n\n                          Noncompliant                             Direct record evidence contradicts a mandatory control. A missing field by itself is not proof of noncompliance.\n\n                          Not established                          A required fact is absent, ambiguous, or cannot be verified from the packet.\n\n                          Recommended practice                     An operational quality expectation. It is reported separately and is not a mandatory-control failure solely because it was not followed.\n\n\n\n Record locators R-01 to R-32 are operational row references only. They are retained to make this packet traceable without identifying a person.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                                             Page 1\n\fGRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                                         Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n 3. Mandatory referral-handling controls\n                          Control family                                            Required evidence\n\n                          IC-1 | Intake information                                 Each referral record must evidence: a unique referral key, date received, referring source, requested service, and destination or\n                                                                                    receiving service.\n\n                          IC-2 | Basis before external disclosure                   Before information is disclosed to an external receiving service, the record must contain a documented authorization or another\n                                                                                    documented operational basis allowed by this internal standard.\n\n                          IC-3 | Routing and receipt                                A transfer sent outside the Referral Operations desk must show the destination and confirmation from the receiving service where\n                                                                                    the referral has been completed. A record still marked Pending receipt at the cut-off needs a destination, current status and\n                                                                                    accountable role; receipt confirmation is not yet due solely because it is pending.\n\n                          IC-4 | External disclosure log                            Where an external disclosure occurred, it must be represented in the applicable access or disclosure log. This control does not\n                                                                                    apply where no external disclosure occurred.\n\n                          IC-5 | Closure or current disposition                     For a Closed or Returned record, show the outcome or disposition, closure date and responsible role. For an Open or Pending\n                                                                                    receipt record, show the current status and accountable role; an outcome and closure date are not due while the referral remains\n                                                                                    open.\n\n\n\n\n 4. Applicability by workflow\n                          Workflow group                                    IC-2 / IC-4                                 IC-3                                               IC-5 at cut-off\n\n                          External transfer - Closed                        Applies if sent externally                  Destination + receiving-service confirmation       Outcome, date, responsible role\n\n                          External transfer - Pending receipt               Applies if external send is recorded        Destination; receipt confirmation not yet due      Current status + accountable role\n\n                          Internal coordination                             Not applicable: no external disclosure      Internal handoff + service acceptance              Closed: outcome/date/role; Open:\n                                                                                                                                                                           status/role\n\n                          Returned before external disclosure               Not applicable                              Not applicable: no transfer occurred               Disposition, date, responsible role\n\n\n\n A later administrative entry does not remedy the sequencing requirement in IC-2. Conversely, an absent or unclear entry is classified as not established unless the record directly shows the mandatory\n requirement was contradicted.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                                           Page 2\n\fGRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                                         Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n 5. Recommended operating practices\n                          Practice                                        Expectation                                                            How to report it\n\n                          RP-1 | Acknowledgement                          Aim to acknowledge the referral within 2 business days after           Record as on target, late, or timing not evidenced. It is not a\n                                                                          receipt.                                                               mandatory-control failure by itself.\n\n                          RP-2 | Reason category                          Use the standard referral-reason category in the operational record.   Record as present or not recorded; treat as a quality improvement\n                                                                                                                                                 point.\n\n                          RP-3 | Completeness check                       Obtain a second-person completeness or quality check where             Record as present or not recorded; do not promote it to a\n                                                                          workload allows.                                                       mandatory control.\n\n                          RP-4 | Supervisory monitoring                   Carry out periodic supervisory review or trend monitoring.             Report available monitoring evidence separately from case-level\n                                                                                                                                                 mandatory control results.\n\n\n\n\n 6. Publication conditions\n                                 A public-facing assessment must be de-identified and traceable to this evidence packet.\n\n                                 A bounded or limited review may support only a bounded assurance statement, with the reviewed coverage and its limitations disclosed.\n\n                                 Material mandatory exceptions or adverse findings must not be omitted.\n\n                                 The assessment must not imply that the full referral population complied when only a subset was reviewed or mandatory evidence remains unresolved.\n\n\n\n Source location guide: controls and evidence terms are on pages 1-2; recommended practices and publication conditions are on page 3; record-register sections follow by workflow group. The report\n date is later than the evidence cut-off and is not an additional evidence date.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                                           Page 3\n\fGRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                                                         Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n 7. Operational record register | external transfer - Closed\n Eight external transfers marked Closed at the evidence cut-off. External disclosure, destination, receipt confirmation and closure evidence are assessed where shown.\n Register key: Intake: 5/5 = key, received date, source, requested service and destination recorded; src- = referring source absent; dest- = destination absent. Basis: ok = documented before external send; after = external send preceded authorization;\n missing = no basis record in packet; n/a = no external disclosure. Route: full = destination + receipt confirmation; receipt- = confirmation absent; pending-ok = destination plus pending status/owner; route-dest- = destination absent; internal-ok = handoff +\n service acceptance; n/a = no transfer. Log: present = applicable external disclosure log entry; extract- = log extract unavailable; n/a = no external disclosure. Close/current: closed-ok = outcome/date/role; date- = closure date absent; ongoing-ok =\n status/role; owner- = accountable role absent. Ack is business days; nr = timing not recorded.\n\n\n                      Row             Workflow / status              Recv'd            Intake / basis                               Route / external log                         Closure / current state        Recommended cues\n\n                      R-01            EXT-CLOSED                     01-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route full                                   closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-02            EXT-CLOSED                     03-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route full                                   closed-ok                      Ack 3 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-03            EXT-CLOSED                     08-Apr-26         Intake src-                                  Route full                                   closed-ok                      Ack 2 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-04            EXT-CLOSED                     16-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route full                                   closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category N\n                                      Closed                                           Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-05            EXT-CLOSED                     24-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route full                                   closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis after (send 10:14; authorization       Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n                                                                                       10:27)\n\n                      R-06            EXT-CLOSED                     05-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route full                                   closed-ok                      Ack nr | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check N\n\n                      R-07            EXT-CLOSED                     12-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route receipt- (destination shown)           closed-ok                      Ack 3 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-08            EXT-CLOSED                     21-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route full                                   closed-ok                      Ack 2 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check N\n\n\n\n Sequence note for R-05: the register records the external send before the authorization entry. This is direct contrary evidence for the timing requirement in IC-2, rather than a missing-field issue.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                                                                   Page 4\n\fGRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                                                         Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n 8. Operational record register | external transfer - Pending receipt\n Eight external transfers awaiting receiving-service confirmation at the evidence cut-off. Receipt confirmation and a closure outcome are not due solely because the status remains pending.\n Register key: Intake: 5/5 = key, received date, source, requested service and destination recorded; src- = referring source absent; dest- = destination absent. Basis: ok = documented before external send; after = external send preceded authorization;\n missing = no basis record in packet; n/a = no external disclosure. Route: full = destination + receipt confirmation; receipt- = confirmation absent; pending-ok = destination plus pending status/owner; route-dest- = destination absent; internal-ok = handoff +\n service acceptance; n/a = no transfer. Log: present = applicable external disclosure log entry; extract- = log extract unavailable; n/a = no external disclosure. Close/current: closed-ok = outcome/date/role; date- = closure date absent; ongoing-ok =\n status/role; owner- = accountable role absent. Ack is business days; nr = timing not recorded.\n\n\n                      Row             Workflow / status              Recv'd            Intake / basis                               Route / external log                         Closure / current state        Recommended cues\n\n                      R-09            EXT-PENDING                    29-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route pending-ok (destination + owner)       ongoing-ok                     Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-10            EXT-PENDING                    02-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route pending-ok (destination + owner)       ongoing-ok                     Ack 4 | category Y\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-11            EXT-PENDING                    04-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route pending-ok (destination + owner)       ongoing-ok                     Ack nr | category Y\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis missing (external send recorded)       Log present                                                                 2nd check N\n\n                      R-12            EXT-PENDING                    09-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route pending-ok (destination + owner)       ongoing-ok                     Ack 2 | category Y\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis ok                                     Log extract-                                                                2nd check Y\n\n                      R-13            EXT-PENDING                    11-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route pending-ok (destination + owner)       ongoing-ok                     Ack nr | category N\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-14            EXT-PENDING                    16-Jun-26         Intake dest-                                 Route route-dest-                            ongoing-ok                     Ack 3 | category N\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check N\n\n                      R-15            EXT-PENDING                    18-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route pending-ok (destination + owner)       ongoing-ok                     Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check Y\n\n                      R-16            EXT-PENDING                    23-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route pending-ok (destination + owner)       ongoing-ok                     Ack 2 | category Y\n                                      Pending receipt                                  Basis ok                                     Log present                                                                 2nd check N\n\n\n\n Pending-receipt rows should not be read as missing a confirmation merely because confirmation has not yet occurred. The destination, pending status and accountable role are the applicable\n routing/current-state evidence at the cut-off.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                                                                   Page 5\n\fGRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                                                         Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n 9. Operational record register | internal coordination\n Eight internal coordination records. There is no external disclosure in this workflow, so IC-2 and IC-4 do not apply; internal handoff and service acceptance are used for IC-3.\n Register key: Intake: 5/5 = key, received date, source, requested service and destination recorded; src- = referring source absent; dest- = destination absent. Basis: ok = documented before external send; after = external send preceded authorization;\n missing = no basis record in packet; n/a = no external disclosure. Route: full = destination + receipt confirmation; receipt- = confirmation absent; pending-ok = destination plus pending status/owner; route-dest- = destination absent; internal-ok = handoff +\n service acceptance; n/a = no transfer. Log: present = applicable external disclosure log entry; extract- = log extract unavailable; n/a = no external disclosure. Close/current: closed-ok = outcome/date/role; date- = closure date absent; ongoing-ok =\n status/role; owner- = accountable role absent. Ack is business days; nr = timing not recorded.\n\n\n                      Row             Workflow / status              Recv'd            Intake / basis                               Route / external log                         Closure / current state        Recommended cues\n\n                      R-17            INTERNAL                       01-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            closed-ok                      Ack 2 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-18            INTERNAL                       14-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            closed-ok                      Ack 4 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check N\n\n                      R-19            INTERNAL                       30-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category N\n                                      Closed                                           Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-20            INTERNAL                       07-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            ongoing-ok                     Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Open                                             Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-21            INTERNAL                       20-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            owner- (open status shown)     Ack nr | category Y\n                                      Open                                             Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check N\n\n                      R-22            INTERNAL                       27-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            closed-ok                      Ack 2 | category N\n                                      Closed                                           Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-23            INTERNAL                       03-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            ongoing-ok                     Ack 3 | category Y\n                                      Open                                             Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-24            INTERNAL                       22-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route internal-ok                            closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Closed                                           Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check N\n\n\n\n Rows R-20, R-21 and R-23 remain Open at the cut-off. An open status is distinct from a record that lacks closure evidence; current status and accountable-role evidence are the applicable requirements.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                                                                   Page 6\n\fGRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                                                         Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n 10. Operational record register | returned before external disclosure\n Eight referrals returned before any external disclosure or transfer. IC-2, IC-3 and IC-4 do not apply; closure/disposition evidence remains required.\n Register key: Intake: 5/5 = key, received date, source, requested service and destination recorded; src- = referring source absent; dest- = destination absent. Basis: ok = documented before external send; after = external send preceded authorization;\n missing = no basis record in packet; n/a = no external disclosure. Route: full = destination + receipt confirmation; receipt- = confirmation absent; pending-ok = destination plus pending status/owner; route-dest- = destination absent; internal-ok = handoff +\n service acceptance; n/a = no transfer. Log: present = applicable external disclosure log entry; extract- = log extract unavailable; n/a = no external disclosure. Close/current: closed-ok = outcome/date/role; date- = closure date absent; ongoing-ok =\n status/role; owner- = accountable role absent. Ack is business days; nr = timing not recorded.\n\n\n                      Row             Workflow / status              Recv'd            Intake / basis                               Route / external log                         Closure / current state        Recommended cues\n\n                      R-25            RETURNED                       06-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-26            RETURNED                       19-Apr-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    closed-ok                      Ack 3 | category Y\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check N\n\n                      R-27            RETURNED                       06-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    date- (outcome + role          Ack 2 | category N\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                      shown)                         2nd check Y\n\n                      R-28            RETURNED                       18-May-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category N\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-29            RETURNED                       02-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    closed-ok                      Ack 2 | category Y\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check N\n\n                      R-30            RETURNED                       12-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    closed-ok                      Ack nr | category Y\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-31            RETURNED                       20-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    closed-ok                      Ack 2 | category Y\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check Y\n\n                      R-32            RETURNED                       28-Jun-26         Intake 5/5                                   Route n/a                                    closed-ok                      Ack 1 | category Y\n                                      Returned                                         Basis n/a                                    Log n/a                                                                     2nd check N\n\n\n\n Returned rows did not proceed to an external destination. Their no-transfer status does not remove the need to document the returned disposition, closure date and responsible role.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                                                                   Page 7\n\fGRANTHILL LABORATORIES                                                                                                                                                           Referral Operations | internal evidence packet\n\n\n\n\n 11. Operational quality and monitoring evidence\n The following entries are included only for the recommended supervisory-monitoring practice. They do not change the mandatory control classification of individual referrals.\n\n                          Month in evidence period                     Evidence in packet                                                   Operational reading\n\n                          April 2026                                   One supervisory trend-review entry is recorded.                      Monitoring evidence present.\n\n                          May 2026                                     No supervisory review entry is included in this packet.              Not evidenced in the packet.\n\n                          June 2026                                    No supervisory review entry is included by the evidence cut-off.     Not evidenced in the packet at cut-off.\n\n\n\n\n 12. Record-register summary\n                          Workflow group                                                               Rows                               Cut-off status boundary\n\n                          External transfer - Closed                                                   R-01 to R-08 (8)                   Closed at cut-off\n\n                          External transfer - Pending receipt                                          R-09 to R-16 (8)                   External transfer made; confirmation pending\n\n                          Internal coordination                                                        R-17 to R-24 (8)                   Five closed; three open at cut-off\n\n                          Returned before external disclosure                                          R-25 to R-32 (8)                   Returned; no external disclosure or transfer\n\n                          Total                                                                        32                                 Operational population represented in this packet\n\n\n\n\n Operational export reference: CRH-RF-Q2-26. This packet is the complete supplied evidence set for the publication assessment; it does not establish facts outside the listed period or cut-off.\n\n\n\n\nCavendish Engineering referral-handling review | Evidence cut-off: 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local                                                                                                                             Page 8\n\f","truncated":false,"note":"PDF 文字提取；可打开原文件查看排版。"}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/cavendish_referral_compliance_assessment.docx","bytes":41586,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/b0b905f68953105e546a30b546717ed3d99297599613ac858e4ad865b5d44488.docx","sha256":"b0b905f68953105e546a30b546717ed3d99297599613ac858e4ad865b5d44488","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Cavendish Engineering's Patient-Referral Handling Review\nCompliance assessment for Genevieve Lindqvist's publication approval decision\nDECISION\nApprove publication only as a limited, de-identified, evidence-qualified assessment of 16 of 32 records. It must disclose the mandatory sequence exception and unresolved evidence; it cannot state that all referrals complied.\nPurpose, evidence and review boundary\nThis assessment helps Genevieve Lindqvist decide whether Cavendish Engineering's patient-referral handling review may be published for a broad audience. The sole evidence base is the supplied control-and-records packet (cavendish_referral_controls_and_records.pdf), covering 01 Apr 2026 to 30 Jun 2026 and evidence available at 30 Jun 2026, 17:00 local (pp. 1-2; p. 8).\nThe labels are used as the packet defines them: compliant means direct support for the applicable mandatory control; not established means the required fact is missing or cannot be verified; noncompliant means direct contrary evidence. These are record-evidence findings under the internal standard, not clinical or legal conclusions.\nFriday's deadline did not permit a case-by-case review of all 32 rows. The fallback was a purposive, risk-directed cohort of 16 rows: 4 external Closed, 4 external Pending receipt, 4 Internal (2 closed and 2 open), and 4 Returned. It covers each workflow, both external-disclosure and no-disclosure paths, all status groups, routine evidence, missing evidence, and the directly contrary sequence. This is proportionate for a publication decision under time pressure, but it leaves 16 rows unreviewed (4 in each workflow group); it is not a population-wide compliance test.\nMandatory-control findings\nControl\nFinding in the reviewed cohort\nSource\nIC-1\nIntake\n14 of 16 directly support all five required intake elements (key, received date, referring source, requested service and destination). 2 are not established: R-03 lacks the referring source and R-14 lacks the destination. Missing evidence is not recorded as a proven breach.\npp. 2, 4-5\nIC-2\nBasis before external disclosure\nApplies to 8 reviewed external transfers: 6 compliant; 1 not established (R-11, no documented basis in the packet); and 1 noncompliant. R-05 records an external send at 10:14 before authorization at 10:27; a later entry does not meet the before-disclosure control.\npp. 2, 4-5\nIC-3\nRouting and receipt\nApplies to 12 rows: 10 compliant and 2 not established (R-07, R-14: receipt confirmation absent for a Closed external transfer; destination absent for a Pending transfer). The 4 Returned rows had no transfer and are not applicable. Pending receipt is not itself missing confirmation at the cut-off when destination, status and owner are recorded.\npp. 2, 4-7\nIC-4\nExternal log\nApplies to 8 reviewed external transfers: 7 compliant and 1 not established (R-12, applicable log extract unavailable). The 8 Internal or Returned rows had no external disclosure, so no log is inferred or required for them.\npp. 2, 5-7\nIC-5\nClosure / current disposition\n14 of 16 are directly supported: Closed/Returned rows show outcome, date and role, or Open/Pending rows show current status and accountable role. 2 are not established: R-21 is Open but has no accountable role; R-27 has outcome and role but no closure date. An open referral is not treated as lacking a completed closure merely because it is open.\npp. 2, 5-7\n\n\nRecommended practices: separate improvement observations\nRP-1's target is acknowledgement within 2 business days. In the reviewed cohort, 10 acknowledgements were on target, 4 were late, and timing was not evidenced for 2. Late or unrecorded timing is a recommended-practice variation only; it does not prove a mandatory referral-handling breach (p. 3; register pp. 4-7).\nRecommended practice\nObserved evidence in the cohort / packet\nRP-2 | Reason category\nRecorded in 14 of 16; not recorded in 2. Improvement opportunity, not a mandatory failure.\nRP-3 | Second-person check\nRecorded in 10 of 16; not recorded in 6. Improvement opportunity, not a mandatory failure.\nRP-4 | Supervisory monitoring\nOne month has a recorded trend review; 2 months are not evidenced in the packet at cut-off. Report as incomplete monitoring evidence, not a case-level mandatory-control breach.\nEvidence summary and limits\nThe 16-row cohort is traceable by privacy-safe register locator: external Closed (p. 4, R-01 to R-08); external Pending receipt (p. 5, R-09 to R-16); Internal (p. 6, R-17 to R-24); and Returned (p. 7, R-25 to R-32). The cohort contains 6 Closed, 4 Pending receipt, 2 Open and 4 Returned records. No patient names, direct identifiers or clinical detail are reproduced here.\nThe strongest adverse evidence is R-05's directly contrary IC-2 sequence. Mandatory evidence is also not established for intake (R-03, R-14), routing (R-07, R-14), external logging (R-12), and closure/current disposition (R-21, R-27). The remaining 16 records were not reviewed case by case. Therefore, this assessment supports no conclusion about whether every referral in the 32-record population was handled correctly.\nPublication approval decision\nApprove publication only in a limited, de-identified, evidence-qualified form. It must state that the assessment reviewed 16 of 32 records, disclose R-05's mandatory before-disclosure exception and the not-established evidence listed above, and avoid any claim that the full referral population complied. On that bounded basis, publication is supportable under the packet's conditions.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is named exactly `cavendish_referral_compliance_assessment.docx` and is present as the required deliverable.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Filesystem name and submitted file metadata.","grader_hint":"Check the top-level submission for the exact filename and DOCX extension."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The DOCX opens successfully and renders as a readable document without corrupted content, missing text, or unusable formatting.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Opening and rendering the submitted DOCX.","grader_hint":"Open and render the document with standard offline office tooling; award credit only if the substantive content is accessible."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment is no more than two rendered pages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render the DOCX with ordinary office defaults and count pages, allowing only normal minor variation from the document's stated settings."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document clearly states that it is assessing Cavendish Engineering’s patient-referral handling review for a publication approval decision and identifies Genevieve Lindqvist or the approving audience.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Opening purpose or executive conclusion.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit purpose and intended decision reader, not merely a generic title such as 'compliance review'."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment identifies the supplied control-and-records packet as its evidence base and states the relevant evidence period or as-of point from that packet.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Scope, evidence-basis, or methodology note.","grader_hint":"Compare the stated source and date boundary with the PDF; do not award credit for an invented review date."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment explains the bounded fallback used in place of a complete case-by-case review and gives a defensible reason why that fallback is proportionate to the deadline and risk.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Scope and approach explanation.","grader_hint":"The document must describe what was actually reviewed and why that coverage is defensible; a bare statement that 'sampling was used' is insufficient."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment states the reviewed coverage, the relevant denominator or population boundary, and the material record pathways or status groups that the fallback does and does not represent.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Coverage statement and evidence summary.","grader_hint":"Compare the stated coverage with the pathways and status groups represented in the PDF; ensure the document does not imply review of unreviewed records."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every mandatory control family identified in the supplied policy is addressed in the assessment rather than being collapsed into a vague overall score.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Control-by-control findings.","grader_hint":"Use the mandatory-control portion of the PDF as the checklist and verify that each family receives an evidence-based disposition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment correctly evaluates the mandatory intake-information control against the records, including the required intake elements defined in the packet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Finding for the intake-information control.","grader_hint":"Compare each stated conclusion with the packet’s intake fields and evidence status; do not accept a conclusion based only on whether a referral exists."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment correctly evaluates the mandatory authorization or documented-basis control before external disclosure.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Finding for authorization or disclosure basis.","grader_hint":"Check whether the assessment distinguishes documented permission or basis before disclosure from later administrative notes, using the source record sequence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment correctly evaluates mandatory routing and receiving-service confirmation evidence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Routing or receipt finding.","grader_hint":"Compare the assessment’s classification with destination and receipt evidence in the packet, including ambiguous or incomplete entries."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment correctly evaluates the mandatory access or external-disclosure logging control where that control applies.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Access or disclosure-log finding.","grader_hint":"Verify that the document does not infer a log merely from a completed referral and does not apply the control where the packet shows it is inapplicable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment correctly evaluates the mandatory closure or disposition control, including the required outcome, date, or responsible-role evidence specified by the packet.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Closure or disposition finding.","grader_hint":"Compare the stated status with the packet’s closure evidence and distinguish an open case from a case whose closure evidence is merely absent."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document uses the policy’s evidence distinctions consistently: direct support is treated as compliant, direct contrary evidence as noncompliant where applicable, and missing or ambiguous evidence as not established rather than silently resolved.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Control findings and case-level explanations.","grader_hint":"Cross-check representative complete, contradictory, and incomplete records in the PDF against the labels used in the assessment."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Recommended practices in the packet are separately identified as recommended or improvement opportunities and are not used alone to declare a mandatory control failure.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Findings concerning recommended practices.","grader_hint":"Check the packet’s recommended-practice language, including timing and process-quality recommendations, against the assessment’s labels and overall conclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment handles the recommended acknowledgement-time expectation accurately, distinguishing lateness or missing timing evidence from proof of a mandatory referral-handling breach.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Timing-related finding.","grader_hint":"Compare the treatment of acknowledgement timing with its classification in the source policy; it should not be promoted to a compulsory failure without source support."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment identifies the material mandatory exception or contrary event present in the packet, if included in the reviewed evidence, and does not dilute it by describing the overall process as fully compliant.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Adverse finding and overall conclusion.","grader_hint":"Locate the packet’s direct contrary mandatory event and verify that the assessment either reports it accurately or transparently explains why it falls outside the reviewed evidence; an unqualified 'fully compliant' claim fails."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment does not generalize the fallback findings to the entire referral population and explicitly limits any assurance claim to the supported scope.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Conclusion, assurance wording, and limitations.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear boundary around reviewed records, pathways, or evidence; statements such as 'all referrals complied' are not acceptable unless the source supports that population-wide claim."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any counts, proportions, or summarized findings in the assessment reconcile with the records and control classifications on which they are based.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Tables, narrative totals, and source record groupings.","grader_hint":"Recalculate stated totals from the cited reviewed set and check that categories are mutually intelligible and not double-counted."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The assessment provides enough traceability for a reviewer to connect material findings to record groups, source sections, or other privacy-safe locators in the supplied PDF.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Citations, source locators, or evidence-reference notation.","grader_hint":"A reader should be able to verify the important findings from the PDF without requiring the author’s private notes; exact patient identifiers are not required."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The assessment minimizes sensitive content while retaining enough evidence for a publication decision; it does not reproduce patient names, direct identifiers, or unnecessary clinical detail.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered document as a whole.","grader_hint":"Review every page for unnecessary patient-level or clinical information and judge whether the evidence summary is appropriately anonymized for a broad audience."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The document avoids unsupported clinical, legal, regulatory, or population-level claims and distinguishes what the operational records can show from what they cannot establish.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Claims throughout the assessment.","grader_hint":"Assess whether conclusions remain within the supplied internal controls and records rather than importing external standards or making clinical judgments."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The assessment gives one clear publication decision that is appropriately bounded under the supplied publication conditions, rather than presenting equal alternative outcomes.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Final decision statement.","grader_hint":"The conclusion should make a single supportable call about publication and state whether it is limited, conditional, or not supportable; it must not hide behind 'more review is needed' alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The final decision is logically consistent with the mandatory findings, recommended-practice treatment, privacy controls, and stated review limitations.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Relationship between findings, limitations, and decision.","grader_hint":"Read from evidence summary through conclusion and test whether the decision follows from the source-supported findings without overstating or suppressing adverse evidence."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The assessment is usable by a broad non-specialist audience: its labels are defined or self-explanatory, its prose is specific, and it closes with the decision rather than an unstructured list of future tasks.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":true,"evidence":"Rendered document and final section.","grader_hint":"Judge practical readability and decision usability, not decorative styling; a technically accurate document that leaves the approver unable to tell what is being recommended should not receive full credit."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is a departmental compliance review of anonymized patient-referral handling records before a public-facing publication decision. The manager must document a proportionate conclusion under incomplete evidence and a short operational deadline without overstating assurance.","difficulty_sources":["Drawing a defensible mandatory-versus-recommended boundary in borderline referral records.","Producing a proportionate fallback assessment when a complete case-by-case review cannot meet the Friday deadline.","Keeping public-facing claims privacy-minimized and limited to what incomplete operational evidence supports."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_file":{"filename":"cavendish_referral_controls_and_records.pdf","construction":"Create one offline-readable PDF that combines a concise internal referral-handling control standard with an anonymized operational record packet. Keep all record identifiers synthetic and non-identifying. The source should be realistic and compact enough for a practitioner to inspect, but contain enough records and variation that a complete case-by-case review is not a reasonable Friday-deadline assumption.","policy_content":{"mandatory_controls":["Required intake information must be evidenced, including a unique referral key, date received, referring source, requested service, and destination or receiving service.","Before an external disclosure, the record must contain a documented authorization or other documented operational basis permitted by the internal standard.","Routing must be evidenced through a destination record and receiving-service confirmation where the control applies.","External access or disclosure must be represented in the applicable access or disclosure log.","Closure must be evidenced through the required disposition or outcome, timing, and responsible-role information."],"recommended_practices":["Acknowledgement within the policy’s stated business-day target.","Use of a standardized referral-reason category.","A second-person completeness or quality check.","Periodic supervisory review or trend monitoring."],"evidence_definitions":["Compliant requires direct support for the applicable control.","Noncompliant requires direct contrary evidence of a mandatory control, not merely a missing field.","Not established is the appropriate evidence status when a required fact is absent, ambiguous, or cannot be verified from the packet.","Recommended practices should be reported separately as recommended, inconsistent, or improvement opportunities and should not be treated as mandatory solely because they are operationally desirable."],"publication_conditions":["A public-facing assessment must be de-identified and traceable to the supplied evidence.","A bounded or limited review may support only a bounded assurance statement with coverage and limitations disclosed.","Material mandatory exceptions or adverse findings must not be omitted.","The assessment must not imply that the full referral population is compliant when the evidence covers only a subset or leaves mandatory evidence unresolved."]},"record_design":{"patterns":["Include records with direct support for all applicable mandatory controls.","Include incomplete records where one or more mandatory evidence elements are absent.","Include at least one record with direct contrary evidence for a mandatory control so the distinction between missing evidence and a proven breach is reachable.","Include records with late or absent recommended acknowledgement, missing standardized categories, or absent second-person checks without making those facts direct mandatory breaches.","Represent each material workflow pathway and relevant referral status group named by the policy so a defensible fallback must consider coverage rather than choosing only convenient records.","Include enough evidence variation for a bounded review to state what was reviewed, what remains unreviewed, and why the conclusion cannot be generalized without qualification."],"traceability":"Give each synthetic record or record group a safe source locator that can be cited in an assessment without exposing patient identity. Keep the source internally consistent so the record evidence, policy definitions, and publication conditions support one coherent intended conclusion."}},"gold_derivation":{"intended_quality":"A strong assessment separates mandatory control findings from recommended-practice observations, marks missing evidence as not established, identifies any directly evidenced mandatory breach, reports the coverage and limitations of a proportionate fallback, and uses privacy-safe traceability.","intended_verdict":"The source should support a single bounded publication call rather than an unqualified full-compliance claim: publication may be supportable only in the limited, de-identified, evidence-qualified form allowed by the packet, with material adverse or unresolved mandatory findings disclosed. The exact wording and whether the recommendation is framed as limited approval or non-approval must follow the source conditions and the evidence, not a fixed sentence.","review_method":"After constructing the PDF, create an independent reference assessment offline and walk every rubric predicate against it. Verify that the mandatory and recommended distinctions, incomplete evidence, direct contrary evidence, coverage groups, and publication conditions are all visible in the source and can be handled without internet access. Confirm that no rubric item requires an invented local code, a hidden authoring fact, or a literal numeric answer."}},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"freeform"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"ref_cavendish_controls_records","filename":"cavendish_referral_controls_and_records.pdf","purpose":"The sole evidence source for the assessment: it contains the internal referral-handling control standard, the mandatory-versus-recommended definitions, publication conditions, and anonymized operational records with incomplete and borderline evidence.","required":true,"discovery":"Open the supplied PDF from the working directory before preparing the assessment."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"compliance_assessment","filename":"cavendish_referral_compliance_assessment.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A concise, privacy-minimized compliance assessment for Genevieve Lindqvist’s publication decision, written for a broad non-specialist audience.","required":true,"constraints":["Write the file into the top level of the starting working directory using exactly the specified filename.","No more than two pages.","Base all factual findings on the supplied PDF.","Distinguish compliant, not established, and contradicted findings.","Do not reproduce patient names, direct identifiers, or unnecessary clinical details.","State one bounded publication decision and its evidentiary limitations."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"evaluate_compliance","work_product":"compliance_assessment","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"medical_health_services_managers","sector":"healthcare_social_assistance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":3.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A domain-informed reviewer should compare the completed assessment with the supplied control standard and anonymized records, then independently inspect the rendered document for scope discipline, privacy minimization, and whether the publication decision follows from the evidence.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The supplied records are synthetic and internally constructed for the assessment.","The task does not require or permit external jurisdiction-specific research.","The rubric evaluates evidence handling and professional usability rather than a fixed page layout or fixed numeric answer."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:50:31+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:50:31+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:50:31+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T15:50:31+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/52aafd6a320b9efa","declared_deliverables":["cavendish_referral_compliance_assessment.docx"]};
